  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> slides on an inclined plane which makes an angle of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>°</mo></math> with the horizontal. The coefficient of friction between the block and the surface is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. The force along the plane that needs to be applied to the block so that it moves up without any acceleration is ( take&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> )",
